      ":question/problem": "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
